512:- [[REDACTED]8:22:20Z] quant-skeptic/verification — ✅ [REDACTED]VERIFY: oshares-vong6-KHEP-CHUOI-verify-doc-lap-xong: {"finding_topic": "oshares-vong6-KHEP-CHUOI-verify-doc-lap-xong", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "pass — no forward columns anywhere in this pipeline; all anchor filters in oshares_live.py are `<= asof` (lines 326, 330, 386, 389). Feed-restatement (vintage) non-reproducibility is the very thing model_version() was added to surface, not hidden. No sizing/NAV/order path touched: commit 898390ad = 4 files, and oshares_live.py/oshares_pit.py/corp_action_lib.py are clean at 8908640 (verified via git status + md5 vs HEAD).", "oos_robustness": "na — operational corp-action publish/alert pipeline, no return series, no IS/OOS split applicable.", "panel_curation_bias": "na — universe is `track = held ∪ ex_today ∪ ais_today`, driven live by holdings and the BQ event calendar; no hardcoded name list. The round's whole subject is precisely that this set rotates.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — I re-ran corp_action_daily_selfcheck.py myself: 153/153 PASS under normal, `env -u TZ`, TZ=America/New_York, TZ=UTC. Working-tree md5 == HEAD for both changed files (51c2a1cb…, ade7c84f…). I re-applied mutation M3 (`&`→`|` at corp_action_daily.py:1107) independently: exactly NW7/NW8/NW9 FAIL and the churn fixture flips to alert:True; file restored and md5 re-verified.", "param_overfit": "na — no tuned numeric parameter introduced. The one threshold-like choice (keeping INVARIANT_SUSPECT inside n_none rather than excluding it) is argued from a blind-spot mechanism, not fitted to data, and is the conservative direction.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — no trade sizing, no ADV interaction; this layer only publishes/withholds a share-count and emits a Discord line.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "fail (scoped to one evidence sentence, does not void the headline) — payload claims 'KHONG co dong AIS/ISS moi cho EVF/SHB, lo nap gan nhat [REDACTED]'. FALSE: BQ has ISS rows for EVF, SHB and TCB with ingested_at = [REDACTED] 15:48:57 UTC (= 22:48 ICT, AFTER the 17:07 ICT snapshot); ingested_at confirmed UTC against CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(). The author's own gate-2 output prints max_ingested_ict [REDACTED]T22:48:57+07:00 — they appear to have quoted max_public_date ([REDACTED]) instead. Everything else adds up: 33 prev tickers ∩ 35 cur = 29 comparable; 1→3 on comparable with total 4/35; alert basis is comparable-restricted in code (line 1135); `== \"NO_MODEL_VALUE\"` literal count == 1 (line 1002); TCB anchor [REDACTED] shares_total_after 7,086,240,414 confirmed in tav2_bq.corporate_action, matching ticker_financial — so ROUND6 §1's corrected mechanism is right.", "cron_timing_selfcorrection": "pass — system TZ is Etc/UTC; crontab `TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh` enters job env only, not the vixie-cron scheduler. Empirical: backup.log 'done [REDACTED]7:00:01Z' for the `0 17` line; daily_retro (`30 17`) mtime 17:46 UTC. So `30 0 * * 1-5` = 00:30 UTC = 07:30 ICT as cron_registry documents, and the missing corp_action_daily.log is 'not fired yet', not 'crashed'."}, "independent_recompute": "Two, both matched. (1) Ran `corp_action_daily.py --asof [REDACTED]14 --dry-run --no-alert` myself — reproduced ROUND6's gate-4b line and the full 🔇 message VERBATIM: '4/35 … so được 1→3 trên 29 mã chung với mốc [REDACTED], Δ+2 MỚI: [EVF, SHB] [vào track set: HRB] [rời track set: DHN]', including the 'CHƯA LOẠI TRỪ ĐƯỢC' tail. (2) Ran the A/B the author never ran: extracted oshares_live.py + corp_action_lib.py at 1e35fba (the code that produced the 08-13 snapshot) and called oshares_at(['EVF','SHB','TCB'],'[REDACTED]') against TODAY's feed. Old code returns EVF AIS_EXACT 704,248,289 / SHB ISS_ESTIMATE 5,377,339,511.75 / TCB AIS_EXACT 7,086,240,414 — byte-identical to the stored snapshot; new code refuses EVF and SHB. This proves 'model tightened, not feed' independently of the (false) 'no new rows' claim, and shows the 08-13 22:48 ICT ISS ingest is inert for these names.", "killer_objection": "model_version() hashes only corp_action_lib.py + oshares_live.py, but check_invariants (corp_action_daily.py:801) and withhold_suspect (:848) — which produce INVARIANT_SUSPECT / value=None, documented cause (b) of n_none in that same function's docstring — live in corp_action_daily.py, outside _model_files(). Retune an invariant threshold and n_none moves while model_changed=False, which emits NO tail at all, silently leaving the reader with 'kiểm feed'. That is exactly the misdiagnosis point 7 was built to prevent, reintroduced for the other of the two causes the same round just took the trouble to separate. The stated justification ('what is selfchecked before publish and what defines the version must be one set') is sound in general but the two sets genuinely diverge here — round 6 itself changed corp_action_daily.py without changing the signature.", "recommended_reruns": ["BLOCKING before archiving: correct ROUND6.md §7 — the row 'BQ: dòng AIS/ISS mới của EVF/SHB? KHÔNG — lần nạp gần nhất [REDACTED]' is false. There ARE ISS rows for EVF/SHB/TCB at ingested_at [REDACTED] 15:48:57 UTC (22:48 ICT), after the 17:07 ICT snapshot; [REDACTED] is max(public_date), a different field. Keep the wrong sentence visible in a ĐÍNH CHÍNH block per the same discipline §1 used, and replace the evidence with the A/B above (old code at 1e35fba vs HEAD on the same feed) — which proves the conclusion outright instead of by elimination.", "Decide explicitly whether corp_action_daily.py belongs in _model_files(). Either add it (and accept that the signature then changes on every alert-text edit), or add a SECOND signature (e.g. `invariant_version`) covering check_invariants/withhold_suspect, or state in the docstring that model_changed=False does NOT exclude an invariant-layer change. Today model_changed=False is silent, which reads as 'same model'.", "Add a selfcheck case pinning the false-negative: two snapshots with identical model_version but a changed invariant threshold that moves n_none — assert the 🔇 text does NOT assert 'feed' as the suspect.", "After 07:30 ICT [REDACTED]14 (already on the author's list, correctly): confirm live that (a) the 🔇 string matches the dry-run, (b) check_retro fires against a real prior_snapshot, (c) the 08-14 snapshot carries model_version. All three are still dry-run-only.", "Việc B (choosing the corporate_action consumer) remains a user decision — unchanged this round, correctly."], "summary": "The shipped work holds up under independent attack. I reproduced 153/153 PASS across four TZ environments, confirmed both changed files match HEAD and that the three number-producing modules are untouched since round 4, re-ran mutation M3 myself (exactly NW7/NW8/NW9 fail, churn fixture flips to alert:True), and reproduced the live [REDACTED]14 dry-run word-for-word including the 🔇 message. The comparable-set discipline is genuinely in the alert path, refused() is genuinely one predicate, and the cron self-correction is right (schedules are UTC because system TZ is UTC; TZ= only reaches the job env). One attack fails: the payload's evidence for point 7 — 'no new AIS/ISS rows for EVF/SHB, latest ingest [REDACTED]' — is factually wrong; BQ shows ISS rows for both ingested at 22:48 ICT on 08-13, after the snapshot, and the script's own gate-2 line prints that timestamp. It looks like max(public_date) was read as the ingest batch. That does not void the conclusion, because I ran the decisive test the report skipped: the pre-ffe4b39 code, against today's feed, reproduces the 08-13 snapshot exactly while today's code refuses EVF/SHB — so the model change is the cause, proven directly rather than by elimination. Fix that sentence before archiving (by §1's own argument about archived wrong explanations getting quoted verbatim) and decide what to do about corp_action_daily.py sitting outside model_version()'s file list, where the invariant-withholding logic that produces the other half of n_none actually lives. No order numbers change; nothing here reaches sizing or NAV."}
